# The assessment of MODEL-ROUTE-010 against this build. The requirement identifier is
# this file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the
# identity is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a
# record registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# MODEL-ROUTE-010: "Telemetry shall record requested and effective profiles at every
# model-assisted check, fix, and workflow step, including backend/executor package,
# model identity, effort, parameters, inherited settings, overrides, rejected
# candidates, selection rationale, usage, cost, latency, retries, and fallback
# lineage."
#
# ModelExecutionTelemetry still carries all thirteen named fields and nothing emits one.
# What changed is why that is a gap. The old entry said nothing outside nomos-model-package
# referenced a profile, so there was no model-assisted step to record telemetry for;
# P40-MODEL-ROUTING-DISPATCH-WIRING made that false. A workflow agent step now resolves a
# declared profile against a declared package set and dispatches to what answers, which is
# a model-assisted workflow step in the requirement's own terms.
#
# So the absence is sharper than it was rather than smaller. Selected_Dispatch is the one
# place in this workspace where a requested profile becomes an effective one -- it holds
# the requested selector, the effort, the declared set it resolved against, and, through
# ProfileResolution::Resolved, the other targets that also satisfied the selector, which is
# the rejected-candidates field by another name. It records none of it and returns a
# DispatchConfig. Every remaining field of the thirteen -- usage, cost, latency, retries,
# fallback lineage -- has no producer anywhere.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/packages/nomos-model-package/src/model_execution_telemetry.rs#ModelExecutionTelemetry
gap: crates/orchestration/nomos-agent-orchestration/src/backend_selection.rs#Selected_Dispatch
